        ("3.3", "Planning and Scheduling", "DDH implements planning through workflow state rather than an unverified calendar claim. Analysis jobs, event/outbox work, notification delivery and recovery actions have lifecycle states, worker processing, retry behavior and audit records so work can be tracked from creation to completion or failure.", "job/event creation; status transitions; queued work; recovery plan requests", "transactional outbox; worker claim/retry; stale-job handling; dead-letter queue; action approval", "Operational status and auditable progress for asynchronous or controlled tasks."),
